impassible.e:
a. Incapable of suffering; inaccessible to harm or pain;
   not to be touched or moved to passion or sympathy; unfeeling, or not
   showing feeling; without sensation.

inasmuch.e:
adv. In like degree; in like manner; seeing that;
   considering that; since; -- followed by as. See In as much as, under
   In, prep.

inferno.e:
n any place of pain and turmoil; 
n a very intense and uncontrolled fire
n (Christianity) the abode of Satan and the forces of evil; where sinners suffer eternal punishment

inflexible.e:
a. incapable of change
a. resistant to being bent; 
s. incapable of adapting or changing to meet circumstances
